    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d577">

                <pb facs="0616" n="498" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">452.11/218: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hammond</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-06-11T19:00:00-04:00">June 11, 1929—7
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>29. Reference Mr. Blake’s letter to you May 15, 1929,<anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d577-f1"/> and your despatch 1163, February 28, 1929. Department is
                    awaiting offer from Spanish Government to settle Moroccan claims on basis of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ad referendum</hi> agreement between Blake and General
                    Jordana. You may discreetly endeavor to expedite action bearing in mind
                    Department’s instruction in its telegram 52, August 9, 1928,<anchor n="31"
                        xml:id="d577-f2"/> concerning claims reserved. Report situation by
                    telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
